   "since": "2026-09-21",
   "unit": null,
   "value": "The National Women’s Business Council (NWBC) was established as an independent advisory council by the Women’s Business Ownership Act of 1988 (Pub. L. 100-533).\r\n\r\nNWBC was created to review the status of women–owned business nationwide; the role of Federal, State and local governments  in assisting and promoting aid to, and the promotion of, women-owned business; data collection  procedures and the availability of data related to women-owned business; and government initiatives  relating to women owned business, including those related to Federal procurement.\r\n",
